+    {
+      "key": "bath",
+      "namespace": "analysis.spectral",
+      "logical_name": "anderson-schur-bath-negative-imaginary-width-moment",
+      "kind": "concept",
+      "title": "Full deleted-site bath controls the stronger spectral moment",
+      "statement": "DRAFT concept backed by an author derivation, not a promoted theorem. For H=A+lambda V on ell^2(Z^3), A nearest-neighbor adjacency and V iid uniform[-1,1], fix x, z=E+i eta, lambda>0, eta>0. With H^(x) the deleted-site compression and b the neighbor-coupling vector, set Sigma=<b,(H^(x)-z)^(-1)b>, a=E+Re Sigma and B=eta+Im Sigma>0. Conditional on all sites except V_x, Im G_xx=B/((lambda V_x-a)^2+B^2). Its conditional first moment is <=pi/(2lambda). For 1<p<infinity and K_p=integral_R(1+u^2)^(-p)du, its conditional p moment is <=K_p B^(1-p)/(2lambda); on |a|<=lambda/2 and B<=lambda/2 it is >=2^(-p)B^(1-p)/lambda. An eta-uniform integrated p moment thus requires a uniform resonance-weighted negative moment of B. No such estimate is supplied here, and the six neighbors are not independent branches.",
+      "proof_text": null,
+      "assumptions": [
+        "lambda>0",
+        "eta>0",
+        "iid uniform[-1,1] site law",
+        "full deleted-site compression",
+        "nearest-neighbor adjacency with zero diagonal",
+        "1<p<infinity"
+      ],
+      "domain": "probability and spectral theory",
+      "source": {
