+    {
+      "key": "goe",
+      "namespace": "analysis.spectral",
+      "logical_name": "free-lattice-ac-does-not-imply-periodic-goe-statistics",
+      "kind": "concept",
+      "title": "Free ac spectrum does not supply periodic-box GOE statistics",
+      "statement": "DRAFT concept backed by an author derivation, not a promoted theorem. Free nearest-neighbor adjacency on Z^3 has absolutely continuous spectral measures. In periodic boxes of odd side L its eigenvalues are 2 sum_j cos(2pi k_j/L), k in (Z/LZ)^3. In any fixed open interval I=(a,b) with -6<a<b<6, k -> -k pairs all momenta and forces at least half of the sorted adjacent spacings to be zero as the bulk count diverges. Strictly monotone unfolding preserves those coincidences, obstructing GOE bulk spacing statistics. This uses lambda=0 and does not refute fixed positive-disorder C0056.",
+      "proof_text": null,
